WEBVTT

00:00.375 --> 00:03.928
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:03.929 --> 00:07.265
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:07.266 --> 00:10.935
♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.936 --> 00:13.966
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.967 --> 00:17.241
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.242 --> 00:20.470
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.471 --> 00:22.201
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.202 --> 00:23.652
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.653 --> 00:28.995
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.118 --> 00:37.371
Thanks for driving me to the
library for story time, Brian.

00:37.372 --> 00:39.830
<i>Today we're reading The
Very Hungry Caterpillar</i>

00:39.831 --> 00:41.403
<i>vs. The Human Centipede.</i>

00:41.404 --> 00:43.357
<i>I heard it's like Alien vs. Predator.</i>

00:43.358 --> 00:44.855
With a little bit more butt eating.

00:44.856 --> 00:47.084
That does sound fun,
but what if I took you

00:47.085 --> 00:49.345
- to a different library today?
- What?

00:49.346 --> 00:52.363
But I like my library. I
met Curious George there.

00:52.364 --> 00:54.687
Mom said he was a puppet,
but she's stupid.

00:54.688 --> 00:56.304
I'm just saying we
should go to the library

00:56.305 --> 00:57.618
at Quahog University

00:57.619 --> 00:59.555
and take your education
to a higher level.

00:59.556 --> 01:02.217
I guess I can try it. I mean,
I do want to get ahead.

01:02.218 --> 01:05.874
I don't want to end up like
Meg, doing sad one-woman shows.

01:05.875 --> 01:09.698
♪ Oh, I love trash ♪

01:09.699 --> 01:13.960
♪ Anything dirty or dingy or dusty ♪

01:13.961 --> 01:18.165
♪ Anything ragged or rotten or rusty ♪

01:18.166 --> 01:22.601
♪ Yes, I love trash... ♪

01:22.602 --> 01:24.136
Whose fault is this?

01:24.137 --> 01:25.972
You're wearing a garbage bag as a cape.

01:25.973 --> 01:27.007
Who do you think?

01:27.008 --> 01:29.723
- Him?
- Shh. She's crushing it!

01:38.451 --> 01:41.003
Oh, yeah. That's good library.

01:41.004 --> 01:43.722
Aw, you didn't come here for
me; you came to be a creep.

01:43.723 --> 01:45.192
Whatever. You go do your thing.

01:45.193 --> 01:47.726
I'm gonna go watch that young
hotshot attorney over there

01:47.727 --> 01:49.996
who's clearly in the
middle of a movie montage.

02:01.358 --> 02:04.228
Oh! He found it.
He's gonna win the case.

02:06.980 --> 02:09.249
Oh, no. It was a '70s movie.

02:20.211 --> 02:22.243
- So, who you reading?
- George Eliot.

02:22.244 --> 02:23.740
Ah, Georgie.

02:23.741 --> 02:24.933
I'm a big fan.

02:24.934 --> 02:26.133
- I think he, uh...
- She.

02:26.134 --> 02:28.268
She said it best when she said...

02:28.269 --> 02:31.004
"Bantam Press, 1851."

02:32.440 --> 02:34.207
- Lumineers?
- What?

02:34.208 --> 02:35.225
Hmm?

02:35.226 --> 02:37.471
You just said "Lumineers"
with no context.

02:37.472 --> 02:39.179
Did I do that?

02:39.180 --> 02:40.532
Ugh!

02:41.698 --> 02:42.815
Tumblr?

02:45.870 --> 02:49.689
Wow, I've never seen someone go
oh for six in 15 minutes before.

02:49.690 --> 02:52.714
Just hard rejection
after hard rejection.

02:55.229 --> 02:57.830
- What's going on over there?
- Looks like a student rally.

02:57.831 --> 02:59.615
They probably forgot
to study for an exam,

02:59.616 --> 03:01.277
so they organized a protest.

03:01.278 --> 03:03.180
In the '90s, you'd just
pull a fire alarm...

03:03.181 --> 03:04.412
Now you hold a protest.

03:04.413 --> 03:07.536
That is, when they're not
looking down at their phones.

03:11.040 --> 03:12.740
Hey, what's going on?

03:12.741 --> 03:14.924
Someone wrote "weird" on
the transgender bathroom,

03:14.925 --> 03:16.926
and the school president
didn't overreact,

03:16.927 --> 03:18.462
so we want him fired!

03:18.463 --> 03:19.797
Seems reasonable.

03:19.798 --> 03:20.864
Exactly!

03:20.865 --> 03:22.366
Oh, I see news cameras.

03:22.367 --> 03:25.756
I'm gonna yell "Viva la Stool"
like a young, white drunkard.

03:26.750 --> 03:29.319
And last week, a professor told
his class to have a nice day,

03:29.320 --> 03:30.420
which is microaggression,

03:30.421 --> 03:32.542
because in our systemic rape culture

03:32.543 --> 03:33.823
no day is a nice day.

03:33.824 --> 03:35.862
So we want him fired, too.

03:35.863 --> 03:37.527
Hey, if you
don't want to get fired,

03:37.528 --> 03:39.295
- don't become a teacher, right?
- Totally.

03:39.296 --> 03:41.884
You should tweet that. #FireEveryone.

03:41.885 --> 03:43.132
Viva la Stool!

03:43.133 --> 03:46.035
Well, I guess I could
fire up my account again.

03:46.036 --> 03:47.437
All right, open app.

03:47.438 --> 03:49.205
Got a bunch of those. No biggie.

03:49.206 --> 03:50.606
Typing tweet.

03:50.607 --> 03:52.108
Blast off in three,

03:52.109 --> 03:53.676
two, one,

03:53.677 --> 03:55.445
and tweeted.

03:55.446 --> 03:58.014
I am back in the game. See?

03:58.015 --> 03:59.615
Oop, you're gone.

03:59.616 --> 04:01.317
And the crowd is gone.

04:01.318 --> 04:02.868
And the animators are gone.

04:08.415 --> 04:10.149
Hey, Stewie, what do you
think about this tweet?

04:10.150 --> 04:11.650
Oh, don't be that guy.

04:11.651 --> 04:13.669
"Kelly Ripa no-shows at work."

04:13.670 --> 04:16.440
Who does she think she is,
a Republican senator?

04:16.441 --> 04:18.799
#G-O-P-U.

04:18.800 --> 04:21.428
Three references in one
tweet. I'm sweating.

04:21.429 --> 04:23.187
I'll just add it to my notes for later.

04:23.188 --> 04:24.815
<i>Why are you getting into Twitter now?</i>

04:24.816 --> 04:27.717
Unless you're an athlete or
a celebrity, no one cares.

04:27.718 --> 04:29.374
A lot of people like my stuff.

04:29.375 --> 04:32.022
Oh, yeah? Someone needs
to tell Donald Trump

04:32.023 --> 04:33.227
it's not fashionable

04:33.228 --> 04:35.426
to wear orange on your
face after Labor Day.

04:35.427 --> 04:37.400
#OompaTrumpa.

04:37.401 --> 04:39.379
Zero retweets. Zero likes.

04:39.380 --> 04:40.888
- Yeah, viral.
- You know, I don't care.

04:40.889 --> 04:42.515
You can't stop me. Just like people

04:42.516 --> 04:44.968
can't stop Peter from
ordering shepherd's pie.

04:44.969 --> 04:46.870
And what can I get for you, sir?

04:46.871 --> 04:48.105
I'll have the shepherd's pie.

04:48.106 --> 04:50.039
I'm sorry, but that's not on the menu.

04:50.040 --> 04:51.875
- Well, do you have potatoes?
- Yes.

04:51.876 --> 04:52.945
- Butter?
- Yes.

04:52.946 --> 04:54.046
- Cream?
- Yes.

04:54.047 --> 04:55.047
- Salt?
- Yes.

04:55.048 --> 04:56.048
- Pepper?
- Yes.

04:56.049 --> 04:57.049
- Garlic?
- Yes.

04:57.050 --> 04:58.117
- Onions?
- Yes.

04:58.118 --> 04:59.217
- Lamb?
- Yes.

04:59.218 --> 05:00.318
- Carrots?
- Yes.

05:00.319 --> 05:01.387
- Eggs?
- Yes.

05:01.388 --> 05:02.455
- Flour?
- Yes.

05:02.456 --> 05:03.556
- Rosemary?
- Yes.

05:03.557 --> 05:04.590
- Thyme?
- Yes.

05:04.591 --> 05:05.658
- Chicken broth?
- Yes.

05:05.659 --> 05:06.726
- Corn?
- Yes.

05:06.727 --> 05:07.792
- Peas?
- Yes.

05:07.793 --> 05:08.793
Lightsaber?

05:09.761 --> 05:12.716
<i>Remember when we did Star Wars?</i>

05:18.653 --> 05:21.841
Better get a tweet out before
I go dark for a few hours.

05:23.031 --> 05:25.677
About to see the new Kevin Hart movie.

05:25.678 --> 05:28.481
Just kidding. I'm white
and went to college.

05:28.482 --> 05:30.768
#BaywatchMovie.

06:29.826 --> 06:31.766
Wow, I haven't seen that much camel toe

06:31.767 --> 06:33.179
since the Arab Spring.

06:33.180 --> 06:35.949
#ThinkingInTweets.

06:37.718 --> 06:39.152
Nah.

06:39.153 --> 06:42.171
Hey, are you @dogbackwards from Twitter?

06:42.172 --> 06:43.792
I am. Are-are you a fan?

06:43.793 --> 06:45.386
You racist jerk!

06:45.387 --> 06:47.739
I hope you get foot-and-mouth disease!

06:47.740 --> 06:49.246
What the hell was that?

06:50.313 --> 06:52.217
Uh-oh.

06:56.154 --> 06:58.472
<i> Wow,
you are blowing up!</i>

06:58.473 --> 07:00.041
<i>Blowing up bad.</i>

07:00.042 --> 07:02.542
<i>Ah, look at that... Huffington
Post just picked it up.</i>

07:02.543 --> 07:03.743
<i>Buckle up, buddy.</i>

07:08.550 --> 07:10.702
- There he is!
- Where? I'm in the back.

07:20.109 --> 07:22.662
<i>Hey, how was Baywatch? I
want to see that bad.</i>

07:22.663 --> 07:24.364
What were you thinking,
writing that tweet?

07:24.365 --> 07:25.865
What? It was just a joke.

07:25.866 --> 07:29.241
Brian, it's not 2005...
You can't just go online

07:29.242 --> 07:30.496
and say whatever you want.

07:30.497 --> 07:32.956
Yeah, remember how mad people
got when DiGiorno tweeted

07:32.957 --> 07:34.241
about domestic violence?

07:34.242 --> 07:36.443
And they're not even a
guy. They're pizza.

07:36.444 --> 07:38.411
All right, all right,
I'll delete the tweet.

07:38.412 --> 07:40.113
You haven't deleted it yet?

07:40.114 --> 07:42.200
What a train wreck!

07:44.534 --> 07:45.553
There. Done. Done.

07:45.554 --> 07:47.020
See? It's done. It's gone.

07:47.021 --> 07:49.259
What about all those people outside?

07:49.260 --> 07:50.457
They'll see that I deleted it,

07:50.458 --> 07:52.032
and it'll all blow over. Trust me.

07:52.033 --> 07:53.594
I hope so, but you never know.

07:53.595 --> 07:57.031
They're still pretty mad at me
down at Dick's Sporting Goods.

07:57.032 --> 07:58.799
Um, what's the name of this place?

07:58.800 --> 08:00.200
Dick's.

08:00.201 --> 08:02.536
A-And what's that say on your shirt?

08:02.537 --> 08:04.404
Dick's.

08:04.405 --> 08:07.196
Can I have two balls... and a helmet?

08:07.197 --> 08:09.109
Hey, you're the guy from the phone.

08:10.211 --> 08:11.711
Start the car, Chris!

08:11.712 --> 08:13.877
- Did you get him, Dad?
- We got him!

08:18.065 --> 08:20.320
Hey, Sid. Happy Mango Monday.

08:20.321 --> 08:21.622
Hmm.

08:21.623 --> 08:24.124
Hmm. Those nighttime
information technology classes

08:24.125 --> 08:26.292
must really be getting to Sid.

08:26.293 --> 08:27.393
Hey, Curt.

08:27.394 --> 08:28.394
Hmm.

08:28.395 --> 08:30.230
Curt? Come on, it's me,

08:30.231 --> 08:32.065
Lunchtime Lois.

08:32.066 --> 08:33.600
Gil, help me out here.

08:33.601 --> 08:34.756
Hmm!

08:34.757 --> 08:37.670
Gil, no! Uh, what about
Barbara? Is she back there?

08:37.671 --> 08:39.380
She can clear this up.

08:39.381 --> 08:40.925
Let me talk to Barbara.

08:40.926 --> 08:42.642
She doesn't want to talk to you, either.

08:42.643 --> 08:43.658
Nobody does...

08:43.659 --> 08:45.813
Not as long as you're living
with that racist dog.

08:45.814 --> 08:47.273
Oh, come on!

08:47.274 --> 08:49.032
It was just a bad joke.

08:49.033 --> 08:50.345
Where's Stanley?

08:50.346 --> 08:52.185
He'll vouch for me. Let
me talk to Stanley.

08:52.186 --> 08:54.921
Or Henry. Somebody help me out here.

08:54.922 --> 08:56.589
- Chip?
- Hmm!

08:56.590 --> 08:58.191
- Karen?
- Hmm!

08:58.192 --> 08:59.692
- JJ?
- Hmm.

08:59.693 --> 09:01.361
- Angela?
- Hmm.

09:01.362 --> 09:02.595
- Tito?
- Hmm!

09:02.596 --> 09:04.430
- Larry?
- Hmm!

09:04.431 --> 09:06.333
You can't freeze me out like this.

09:06.334 --> 09:08.301
We're on a first-name basis!

09:08.302 --> 09:10.304
They're on our name tags, Lois.

09:10.305 --> 09:12.940
But I don't even have
to look!

09:12.941 --> 09:16.227
I don't even have to look!

09:22.128 --> 09:24.517
Hey, how come no one told me
we were going to the Clam?

09:24.518 --> 09:25.985
Hey, Jerome, give me a beer.

09:25.986 --> 09:28.188
Oh, why? 'Cause I'm, like, your slave?

09:28.189 --> 09:31.025
Man, you're no better
than your racist dog.

09:31.026 --> 09:32.026
Come on, man.

09:32.027 --> 09:33.960
B-Brian was just making a joke.

09:33.961 --> 09:36.718
I told you about Brian. I told you.

09:36.719 --> 09:38.331
Come on, he deleted his tweet.

09:38.332 --> 09:41.613
But the hurt has been
RT'd in our hearts.

09:41.614 --> 09:42.802
Peter, you better get out of here

09:42.803 --> 09:45.138
before I start saying "sir" like a cop.

09:45.139 --> 09:47.074
- Come on, Joe, I...
- Sir? Sir?

09:47.075 --> 09:48.242
You've been asked to leave.

09:48.243 --> 09:49.977
- Joe, it's me, Peter. I...
- Sir.

09:49.978 --> 09:52.146
I don't want to have to ask you again.

09:52.147 --> 09:53.980
- Please leave.
- All right, fine.

09:53.981 --> 09:55.248
- Sir!
- No, Joe, Joe.

09:55.249 --> 09:56.316
- He's leaving.
- Sir!

09:56.317 --> 09:57.417
- Joe, Joe...
- Sir!

09:57.418 --> 09:58.702
- He's gone.
- Sir.

09:58.703 --> 10:00.204
- It's okay.
- Sir.

10:00.205 --> 10:01.205
He's gone.

10:09.746 --> 10:12.057
Your dog wrote an insensitive tweet.

10:12.058 --> 10:13.366
You can't eat here.

10:13.367 --> 10:15.536
Uh-oh, Meg. It's a sensitivity mob.

10:15.537 --> 10:17.103
It was just a joke.

10:17.104 --> 10:19.205
There's no such thing as jokes anymore.

10:19.206 --> 10:21.274
Yeah, we live in a post-joke world.

10:21.275 --> 10:23.344
Chris, maybe we should just eat outside.

10:23.345 --> 10:25.579
No, Meg, we're eating here.

10:25.580 --> 10:27.899
I'd like to see you try.

11:51.543 --> 11:54.689
It was... a joke.

12:02.477 --> 12:04.478
Can you put on the Canucks game?

12:04.479 --> 12:05.812
No, go away.

12:06.684 --> 12:07.837
Loser.

12:07.838 --> 12:09.555
This is getting out of control.

12:09.556 --> 12:11.618
We can't leave the house
without getting harassed.

12:11.619 --> 12:13.686
Yeah, yesterday I went outside
to try to get the mail

12:13.687 --> 12:14.954
and I had a seizure.

12:14.955 --> 12:16.956
That may not be protester-related,

12:16.957 --> 12:19.203
but still, you got to
do something, Brian.

12:19.204 --> 12:20.303
What do you want me to do?

12:20.304 --> 12:22.396
I-I deleted my Twitter
account, my Instagram,

12:22.397 --> 12:23.564
Facebook, everything.

12:23.565 --> 12:25.465
People still won't leave me alone.

12:25.466 --> 12:27.066
You have to apologize.

12:27.067 --> 12:28.801
Go outside, do it now.

12:28.802 --> 12:31.529
Tell them that it was a
mistake and how sorry you are

12:31.530 --> 12:32.899
and maybe they'll get off our backs.

12:32.900 --> 12:34.568
Maybe you're right.

12:34.569 --> 12:36.870
I got to face them and
hope they'll forgive me.

12:41.017 --> 12:42.285
Hello.

12:42.286 --> 12:44.877
As you all know, I'm Brian Griffin.

12:44.878 --> 12:46.213
Boo.

12:46.214 --> 12:48.781
Boo, Brian Griffin. Boo.

12:48.782 --> 12:50.150
I want to read a few words...

12:50.151 --> 12:51.584
Boo. Liar.

12:51.585 --> 12:54.655
Boo, Brian Griffin, boo.

12:54.656 --> 12:56.182
Anyway, I-I want to...

12:56.183 --> 12:57.790
Boo. Apologize somewhere else.

12:57.791 --> 13:01.727
Boo. Boo, Brian, boo.

13:01.728 --> 13:04.563
Ladies and gentlemen, I'm
here today to apologize...

13:04.564 --> 13:06.505
Why did you say "ladies" first?

13:06.506 --> 13:07.633
That's sexist.

13:07.634 --> 13:09.502
It's just, it's just
a-a standard greeting.

13:09.503 --> 13:12.238
Let-let me start over.
Gentlemen and ladies...

13:12.239 --> 13:13.786
Ooh, says the man.

13:13.787 --> 13:16.819
Okay, sorry, I-I... Um,
humans in the audience...

13:16.820 --> 13:18.911
I identify as a basketball.

13:18.912 --> 13:20.313
Humans and basketballs...

13:20.314 --> 13:21.847
I'm a parrot who mimics words

13:21.848 --> 13:23.183
but doesn't comprehend them.

13:23.184 --> 13:25.584
Humans, basketballs, talking parrots,

13:25.585 --> 13:27.470
and-and whatever else is out there...

13:27.471 --> 13:29.522
"Whatever"? It's whoever.

13:29.523 --> 13:31.157
Actually, it's whomever.

13:31.158 --> 13:32.958
No one likes you, Mary.

13:33.976 --> 13:35.529
All right, all right,
just-just calm down, okay?

13:35.530 --> 13:37.192
Now you're tone policing us!

13:37.193 --> 13:38.765
That makes me uncomfortable.

13:38.766 --> 13:41.601
Anything that makes me
uncomfortable in 2017

13:41.602 --> 13:42.769
should be illegal.

13:42.770 --> 13:45.604
You know what? (BLEEP) you.

13:45.605 --> 13:48.149
I'm not a racist, all right?
I just told a bad joke.

13:48.150 --> 13:49.488
There's a huge difference.

13:49.489 --> 13:51.110
But nobody on the Internet
ever takes the time

13:51.111 --> 13:53.479
to ask themselves, "Is this
worth freaking out over?"

13:53.480 --> 13:56.515
Or, "Are there bigger problems
in the world than this tweet?"

13:56.516 --> 13:57.983
Well, I assure you, there are.

13:57.984 --> 14:00.453
And just for the record,
I love black people.

14:00.454 --> 14:02.188
I watch tons of black porn.

14:02.189 --> 14:04.056
So, what do you all want from me, huh?

14:04.057 --> 14:05.330
You-you want to ruin my life?

14:05.331 --> 14:07.101
Then congratulations. You did it.

14:07.102 --> 14:08.194
Everybody hates me.

14:08.195 --> 14:10.197
I can't leave the house
without getting harassed.

14:10.198 --> 14:11.464
No one will hire me.

14:11.465 --> 14:12.799
That was a problem before.

14:12.800 --> 14:15.068
I can't turn on my phone
without strangers telling me

14:15.069 --> 14:17.525
to kill myself or that they're
gonna kill my family.

14:17.526 --> 14:18.637
Leave me alone!

14:18.638 --> 14:21.474
I'm the self-righteous,
liberal douchebag, not you!

14:21.475 --> 14:23.576
I've kissed a transsexual before!

14:23.577 --> 14:24.810
How many of you can say that?!

14:24.811 --> 14:26.150
Where's my (BLEEP) medal?!

14:26.151 --> 14:27.546
I am so far left,

14:27.547 --> 14:29.849
I'm spinning in circles, you (BLEEP).

14:29.850 --> 14:32.518
Instead of killing myself,
I should kill all of you!

14:32.519 --> 14:34.253
I'd like to see you try.

14:44.547 --> 14:47.517
Ow! Jeez.

14:51.522 --> 14:53.173
Well, we started the dialogue.

14:53.174 --> 14:55.708
You screamed "black porn"
at the top of your lungs

14:55.709 --> 14:57.276
in front of women and children.

14:57.277 --> 14:59.845
I am not the person those
people out there say I am.

14:59.846 --> 15:02.114
I know that, but you
also haven't done much

15:02.115 --> 15:03.349
to prove that you aren't.

15:03.350 --> 15:05.084
I know, I know.

15:05.085 --> 15:06.780
All I have left is you guys.

15:07.273 --> 15:08.688
Thank God you have my back.

15:08.689 --> 15:10.790
- We think you should move out.
- What?!

15:10.791 --> 15:13.693
Oh! Brian, listen, we love you,

15:13.694 --> 15:15.728
but they're throwing
things at our house.

15:15.729 --> 15:18.004
We've got to keep our family safe.

15:18.005 --> 15:20.281
I'm sorry. It's for the best.

15:20.282 --> 15:22.468
Are you serious?!
You're okay with this?!

15:22.469 --> 15:24.938
Does this slow pan across
our disapproving faces

15:24.939 --> 15:26.224
answer your question?

15:36.799 --> 15:38.260
<i>I saw Baywatch.</i>

15:38.261 --> 15:39.894
That thing was frickin' rad.

15:45.270 --> 15:47.122
I still think this is a drastic measure.

15:47.123 --> 15:48.332
Yeah, I messed up,

15:48.333 --> 15:50.332
but what about all the
stupid things Peter's done?

15:50.333 --> 15:52.293
He's never been kicked
out and his life...

15:52.294 --> 15:53.890
My life is not the issue here.

15:53.891 --> 15:55.145
Peter, calm down.

15:55.146 --> 15:56.481
Did you eat breakfast this morning?

15:56.482 --> 15:58.116
I had a banana and a coffee.

15:58.117 --> 15:59.942
Why am I so fat?

15:59.943 --> 16:03.121
I'm sorry, Brian, but this
is the way it has to be.

16:03.122 --> 16:04.338
All right, then.

16:04.968 --> 16:06.621
I guess this is good-bye.

16:14.983 --> 16:16.567
Brian, wait.

16:17.921 --> 16:19.280
This collar is ours.

16:19.281 --> 16:20.704
It has our address on it.

16:20.705 --> 16:22.053
Peace, dude.

16:30.532 --> 16:33.866
All right, radio, time for you
to tell me what this all means.

16:33.867 --> 16:35.986
♪ I got a pocket full of quarters ♪

16:35.987 --> 16:38.673
♪ And I'm headed to the arcade ♪

16:40.874 --> 16:42.659
♪ I don't have a lot of money ♪

16:42.660 --> 16:45.346
♪ But I'm bringing ev'rything I made ♪

16:47.615 --> 16:49.399
♪ I've got a callus on my finger ♪

16:49.400 --> 16:52.420
♪ And my shoulder's hurting, too ♪

16:54.088 --> 16:56.406
♪ I'm gonna eat them all up ♪

16:56.407 --> 16:59.361
♪ Just as soon as they turn blue ♪

17:01.095 --> 17:03.513
♪ 'Cause I've got Pac-Man fever ♪

17:03.514 --> 17:05.215
♪ Pac-Man fever ♪

17:05.216 --> 17:06.750
♪ It's driving me crazy ♪

17:06.751 --> 17:08.051
♪ Driving me crazy ♪

17:08.052 --> 17:10.053
♪ I've got Pac-Man fever ♪

17:10.054 --> 17:11.621
♪ Pac-Man fever ♪

17:11.622 --> 17:13.041
♪ I'm going out of my mind. ♪

17:28.655 --> 17:30.774
<i>Hey. Are you here for the Time magazines</i>

17:30.775 --> 17:32.142
with some of the letters cut out?

17:32.143 --> 17:35.504
Uh, no, I... no, I saw that you
have an apartment for rent.

17:35.505 --> 17:36.546
Okay.

17:36.547 --> 17:38.664
Here. Apartment 23.

17:38.665 --> 17:39.817
Oh, okay.

17:39.818 --> 17:43.120
I just have one rule here:
no kissing the mailman.

17:43.121 --> 17:44.821
I don't think that's gonna be a problem.

17:44.822 --> 17:47.324
You haven't seen him,
so don't say that yet.

17:47.325 --> 17:48.592
Mail's here.

17:48.593 --> 17:50.745
Wow.

18:40.311 --> 18:42.130
If I have other
items I want to buy,

18:42.131 --> 18:44.114
uh, can I buy them here
at the pharmacy window?

18:44.115 --> 18:45.282
Yes.

18:45.283 --> 18:47.450
Ruth? Yeah,
bring it over here.

18:47.451 --> 18:48.819
We can buy them over here.

18:48.820 --> 18:50.120
Where are you?

18:50.121 --> 18:51.188
By the pharmacy.

18:51.189 --> 18:54.202
Hang on, I'm
picking out sunscreen.

18:54.203 --> 18:55.992
Sir, do you
mind if I go ahead of you?

18:55.993 --> 18:58.228
Uh, yes, I do mind.

18:58.229 --> 19:03.485
♪ This time I have really
lead myself astray... ♪

19:10.308 --> 19:13.578
♪ Wrong way on a one-way track ♪

19:13.579 --> 19:17.747
♪ Seems like I should
be getting somewhere ♪

19:17.748 --> 19:21.985
♪ Somehow I'm neither
here nor there... ♪

19:23.988 --> 19:25.889
Six dollars?

19:28.092 --> 19:30.660
Hey, did you knock over a
few bottles in aisle seven?

19:30.661 --> 19:32.396
Uh, yeah.

19:35.166 --> 19:36.531
Okay.

19:43.024 --> 19:44.774
Patricia?

19:44.775 --> 19:46.710
Where's the big nail clipper?

19:46.711 --> 19:47.778
I don't know.

19:47.779 --> 19:49.079
Did you get rid of it?

19:49.080 --> 19:50.247
Why would I get rid
of the big nail clipper?

19:51.949 --> 19:54.117
'Cause you're a bitch, that's why.

19:54.118 --> 19:56.286
Nice. Yeah, now I'm
gonna tell you where it is.

19:56.287 --> 19:58.388
I knew you knew
where it was, you liar.

19:58.389 --> 19:59.556
Tell me where it is!

19:59.557 --> 20:01.058
No. Find it yourself.

20:01.059 --> 20:02.592
Oh, okay. Fine.

20:02.593 --> 20:04.728
How about I hide something
of yours?! Huh?!

20:04.729 --> 20:06.129
Put that back!

20:06.130 --> 20:09.050
No, tell me where
the big nail clipper is!

20:17.892 --> 20:19.542
Boom.

20:19.543 --> 20:21.745
Damn it.

20:21.746 --> 20:24.114
Why can't you
use the little nail clipper?

20:24.115 --> 20:25.750
I want
the big one, okay?!

20:25.751 --> 20:27.784
And I don't want you using it anymore!

20:27.785 --> 20:29.219
Shut up, little man!

20:29.220 --> 20:30.221
You shut up!

20:30.222 --> 20:33.456
Where'd you put it, you liar?!

20:40.749 --> 20:42.561
<i>- $900.
- "L."</i>

20:42.562 --> 20:44.234
- "R."
- Aw.

20:44.235 --> 20:45.669
<i> Two "R" s.</i>

20:48.298 --> 20:54.298
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru